They had come to expect extra respect, even deference from all Iranians, from Shushin Boy to Shah. American lifestyles had come to be imposed as an ideal, the ultimate goal. American books, magazines, films that swept over our country like a flood and we found ourselves wandering, is there any room for our own culture? And I think this is very common in the 60s and 70s across the developing world. But it's especially pronounced in Iran, which has been transformed so much by all of this money. And which has such an ancient culture and such a distinctive culture. Of course.
他们开始期待额外的尊重，甚至是从所有伊朗人那里获得顺从，从擦鞋童到沙阿。美国的生活方式被强加为一种理想，一种终极目标。美国书籍、杂志、电影像洪水一样席卷我们的国家，我们发现自己感到迷茫，我们的文化还有生存空间吗？我认为这在60年代和70年代的发展中国家非常普遍。但在伊朗尤为明显，因为这里被这些金钱改变得太多了。而且它拥有如此古老且独特的文化。当然。

119
00:59:40.000 --> 01:00:35.000
Now, it's no accident. Massimo Eptekar, the woman who wrote those words, was a student. And thanks to the Shah's modernisation project, there are now 200,000 students in Tehran and the other big cities. I mean, that's a rookie's era for a dictator, isn't it? Yeah, create this class of people, educated people, whose ambitions are not being met. Now some of them turn to socialism or communism, but most don't, because if you are feeling alienated and frustrated, given the importance the clerics have always had and the place of Islam in Iran's history, if you are looking for meaning and order and solace and all of those kinds of things, Islam offers you more authentically Iranian answers than socialism and communism do. something is brewing, you know, things are brewing in the kind of tower blocks and in the university campuses and things as the 70s continue.
这绝非偶然。写下这些话的马苏梅·埃布特卡尔当时是一名学生。多亏了沙阿的现代化项目，现在德黑兰和其他大城市有20万名学生。我的意思是，这对独裁者来说是一个菜鸟时代，不是吗？是的，创造了这样一个阶层，受过教育的人，但他们的抱负却无法实现。现在他们中的一些人转向社会主义或共产主义，但大多数人没有，因为如果你感到疏离和沮丧，考虑到教士在伊朗历史上一直拥有的重要地位和伊斯兰教的地位，如果你在寻找意义、秩序、慰藉以及所有这些东西，伊斯兰教为你提供的答案比社会主义和共产主义更具伊朗本土特色。你知道，随着70年代的继续，在那些塔楼公寓和大学校园里，某种东西正在酝酿。

120
01:00:35.000 --> 01:01:13.000
But in Washington, people just don't notice this. And one reason they don't notice is if you're American, you know, you're interested in foreign policy in the early 1970s, you're not looking at Iran, you're looking at Vietnam, in Southeast Asia or Soviet Union or Eastern Europe or Cuba or something. Even in the US embassy, the staff at the US embassy, they had lots of links to the Shah's court, obviously, but not to opposition groups or to the clerics. So I mentioned William Sullivan, the ambassador. When he arrived in 1977, I mean, he wrote this really kind of caustic memoir about his time. He said, I was shocked how few of my colleagues spoke Farsi, how few of them
但在华盛顿，人们根本没有注意到这一点。他们没注意到的一个原因是，如果你是美国人，你对70年代初的外交政策感兴趣，你关注的不是伊朗，而是越南、东南亚、苏联、东欧或古巴之类的地方。即使在美国大使馆，美国大使馆的工作人员显然与沙阿的宫廷有很多联系，但与反对派团体或教士们却没有联系。所以我提到了大使威廉·沙利文。当他在1977年抵达时，他写了一篇关于他那段时光的非常尖刻的回忆录。他说，我感到震惊的是，我的同事中很少有人会说波斯语，很少有人

121
01:01:13.000 --> 01:01:55.000
had ever been outside the capital. So in other words, the information that's getting back to Washington, a lot of it is wrong. And when Carter arrives, you know, the palace for that New Year's Eve dinner. He doesn't realize anything is wrong. He thinks the Shah is going to be there for decades and nothing could possibly go wrong. But actually, just a week after Carter leaves, that's when things start to kick off. Because in recent months, these tapes of Khomeini sermons have been flooding into the markets of Iran and his rhetoric is more and more ferocious. He says the Shah is a Zionist agent, a Jewish agent. He says the Shah is an American serpent. He says people should stop paying tax. They just stop going to school or university or whatever.
去过首都以外的地方。换句话说，传回华盛顿的信息中，很多都是错误的。当卡特到达时，你知道，在那个新年前夜的晚宴上。他没有意识到出了什么问题。他认为沙阿会统治几十年，不可能出任何差错。但实际上，就在卡特离开一周后，事情就开始爆发了。因为近几个月来，这些霍梅尼讲道的录音带不断涌入伊朗的市场，他的言辞越来越凶猛。他说沙阿是犹太复国主义的代理人，是犹太人的代理人。他说沙阿是美国的毒蛇。他说人们应该停止纳税。他们只是停止去学校或大学等等。

122
01:01:55.000 --> 01:02:22.000
This drives the Shah mad. So he waits for Carter to leave, and on the 7th of January, he gets one of the biggest papers in Iran, Etalaat, to publish a repost. And this article, one of the most incendiary articles in any paper in any country in the world in the 20th century, is a full-blooded attack on Khomeini. It says Khomeini is a tool of red and black imperialism. What it means by that is he's been controlled both.
这让沙阿发疯了。所以他等卡特离开，在1月7日，他让伊朗最大的报纸之一《埃特拉特报》发表了一篇反驳文章。这篇文章是20世纪任何国家任何报纸中最具煽动性的文章之一，是对霍梅尼的全面攻击。它说霍梅尼是红色和黑色帝国主义的工具。它的意思是，他一直受到这两者的控制。

123
01:02:22.000 --> 01:02:40.000
both by the communists and by the British. This is a fairly standard kind of theme of Iranian invective. It's good to see the British still. Yeah, it's always the British, right? So are the British black? We're the black imperialists in league with the red imperialist in Moscow. That's the Shah's thinking. This article says, Khomeini's always been into poetry.
既受共产主义者控制，也受英国人控制。这是伊朗式谩骂中相当标准的主题。很高兴看到英国人还在其中。是的，总是英国人，对吧？那么英国人是黑色的吗？我们是与莫斯科的红色帝国主义勾结的黑色帝国主义者。这就是沙阿的想法。这篇文章说，霍梅尼一直喜欢诗歌。

124
01:02:40.000 --> 01:02:55.000
That's a bad sign. It is a bad sign. I mean, everyone in the CIA knows that. It's a really bad sign. It says his ancestry, he's not even really Iranian. He's actually Indian. So he's a foreigner. And it says he's typical of the class, actually.
这是一个坏兆头。这确实是个坏兆头。我的意思是，中情局的每个人都知道这一点。这真的是个坏兆头。它说他的血统，他甚至不是真正的伊朗人。他实际上是印度人。所以他是个外国人。而且它说他实际上是那个阶层的典型。

125
01:02:55.000 --> 01:03:25.000
A lot of these rural clerics are, and I quote, parasites engaged in sodomy, usury, and they're drunk most of the time. So this is what this article says. And this is an absolutely catastrophic own goal. Because within hours of this article, this newspaper reaching the newsstands, there are huge protests in the city of Gom, which is the seminary city where the Ayatollah had been a student and then a teacher. and the seminar is shut down and all the religious students pour out onto the streets to sort of protest about this.
很多这些农村教士都是，我引用一下，“从事鸡奸、高利贷的寄生虫，而且他们大部分时间都在酗酒。”这就是这篇文章所说的。这是一个绝对灾难性的乌龙球。因为在这篇文章见报后的几个小时内，库姆市就爆发了大规模抗议，那是阿亚图拉曾经作为学生和老师所在的宗教城市。神学院被关闭，所有的宗教学生涌上街头进行抗议。

126
01:03:25.000 --> 01:03:40.000
There were demonstrations outside the police station. The police end up firing into the crowds. There's a stampede. And then a number of people who either shot or trampled to death. So this is all January 1978.
警察局外发生了示威。警察最终向人群开火。发生了踩踏事件。然后一些人要么被枪杀，要么被踩死。所以这一切都发生在1978年1月。

127
01:03:40.000 --> 01:03:54.000
Now how many people were shot or trampled to death? Reports at the time said maybe 30, 40. The historian Michael Axeworthy is written a brilliant book on the Iranian Revolution, so it's actually almost all these reports probably exaggerated and it might have been like five people.
那么有多少人被枪杀或踩死？当时的报道说可能有30到40人。历史学家迈克尔·阿克斯沃西写了一本关于伊朗革命的精彩著作，他说实际上所有这些报道可能都被夸大了，可能只有五个人左右。

128
01:03:54.000 --> 01:04:10.000
It doesn't really matter though, does it? It doesn't, exactly, it doesn't matter. Because what matters is that this has happened. Of course. And now what happens is this strange cycle. After 40 days, there are meant to be memorial services for people who've died. So 40 days after these deaths,
但这并不重要，不是吗？确实，完全不重要。因为重要的是这件事已经发生了。当然。现在发生的是这种奇怪的循环。40天后，人们要为死者举行追悼会。所以这些死亡事件发生40天后，

129
01:04:10.000 --> 01:04:27.000
on the 18th of February, there were these memorial services. And there are more demonstrations at universities across Iran. There's a demonstration, for example, in Tabriz, which is close to the border with Soviet Azerbaijan. There, too, the crowd kicks off. There are scuffles.
在2月18日，举行了这些追悼会。伊朗各地的大学里有更多的示威活动。例如，在大不里士发生了一场示威，那里靠近苏联阿塞拜疆的边界。在那里，人群也爆发了。发生了冲突。

130
01:04:27.000 --> 01:04:44.000
There are attacks on cinemas. There are attacks on banks and the symbols of kind of Western influence. The army is sent in. More people are shot. Again, unclear exactly how many. So 40 days after that, these people have memorial services, and you have more riots. And so you have this cycle.
电影院遭到袭击。银行和西方影响的象征遭到袭击。军队被派往那里。更多人被枪杀。同样，不清楚具体有多少人。所以40天后，这些人举行了追悼会，又发生了更多的骚乱。所以就有了这个循环。

131
01:04:44.000 --> 01:05:01.000
Every 40 days, there are memorial services for the people who were killed in the last sort of outbreak of rioting and there's more rioting and so there'll be more memorial services in 40 days' time. So this continues till mid-May. Now the Shah contemplating all this, he makes some concessions.
每40天，人们就会为上次骚乱中丧生的人举行追悼会，然后会有更多的骚乱，所以40天后又会有更多的追悼会。这种情况一直持续到5月中旬。现在沙阿考虑这一切，他做出了一些让步。

132
01:05:01.000 --> 01:05:15.000
He thinks, well, I'll buy the protesters off. He fires the head of the secret police. He says, we can have free elections to the Iranian parliament next year. But he doesn't really get. The Shah is just as detached in many ways as the Americans are. He says, I think this is probably
他想，好吧，我会用钱收买抗议者。他解雇了秘密警察头子。他说，明年我们可以举行伊朗议会的自由选举。但他真的不明白。沙阿在很多方面和美国人一样脱离现实。他说，我想这很可能是

133
01:05:15.000 --> 01:05:31.000
being masterminded by the communists and almost certainly the British. Brilliant. So we're still on the scene again. Again, this mad kind of anglophobia. Now, his courtiers are baffled why the Shah is so... The Shah seems very listless during all this.
由共产主义者策划的，几乎可以肯定是英国人。太棒了。所以我们又回到了现场。又是这种疯狂的恐英症。现在，他的朝臣们很困惑为什么沙阿如此……沙阿在这一切过程中显得非常无精打采。

134
01:05:31.000 --> 01:05:53.000
He's kind of slightly disengaged. They can't understand why he hasn't cracked down much harder. And why actually he's absent from public life and he's spending a lot of his time in his palace at the Caspian Sea. And one reason for this is that what a lot of the Shah's advisors don't know is that he is actually desperately ill.
他有点心不在焉。他们无法理解为什么他没有采取更严厉的镇压措施。以及为什么他实际上缺席了公共生活，大部分时间都待在里海的宫殿里。原因之一是，许多沙阿的顾问不知道的是，他实际上病得很重。

135
01:05:53.000 --> 01:06:33.000
Four years earlier he'd been swimming, he'd noticed a swelling in his side. And his doctors have brought in a French specialist who diagnosed leukemia, the Shah had leukemia. But unbelievably, the Shah's doctors didn't have the courage to tell him. They told him, oh, it's a, you've got a minor blood condition. In 1978, they still haven't really. told him. He seems completely depressed, but they've hidden from him the nature of his condition, although they have told his wife, Empress Farah. Now, there are rumours at this point spreading through Tehran. There's something wrong with the Shah. He looks really kind of gaunt. He's lost a lot of
四年前他游泳时，注意到侧腹有肿块。他的医生请来了一位法国专家，诊断出是白血病，沙阿患有白血病。但令人难以置信的是，沙阿的医生没有勇气告诉他。他们告诉他，哦，这只是一个小小的血液问题。在1978年，他们仍然没有真正告诉他。他看起来完全抑郁了，但他们对他隐瞒了他的病情性质，尽管他们告诉了他的妻子法拉皇后。现在，德黑兰流传着谣言。沙阿出了问题。他看起来真的很憔悴。他瘦了很多

136
